pastex (2.17.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop "Conflicts" and "Replaces" for the retired paste-teks package. With
    "Provides" already gone, the control file now names no other package at
    all: Pastex is self-contained and relates to nothing else.
  * Consequence, stated plainly: on a machine that still has paste-teks
    installed, dpkg may refuse the upgrade because both packages place files
    under the same paths. Removing the old package first clears it:
        sudo apt remove paste-teks
    This is not detected by a field any more, so it can only be reported by
    dpkg at install time.
  * A test asserts that Provides, Conflicts, Replaces and Breaks are all
    absent, in debian/control, in build-deb.sh and in the built .deb.

