pastex (2.13.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A browser start with an empty queue no longer reads Drive. The 3-second
    cache warm-up is gone: the cache already holds the whole library, so a
    start touches Drive only when a queued change has to be sent.
  * One connection per flush. A queue of ten writes used to fetch ten OAuth
    tokens and read the root folder ten times; the flush now connects once and
    reuses the session, and the session follows the index label it writes so a
    reorder and a fold in the same flush no longer overwrite each other.
  * A body that failed to load is retried by the fill pass. It used to be
    skipped forever because the failure was read as "in flight".
  * Cleanup: the unused move command, remap, parentIdOf and the FRESH_MS /
    MAX_LOCAL exports are gone, the duplicated LRU prune is one function, and
    the comments that described removed machinery were corrected.

