pastex (2.13.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read everything from the cache. The library is downloaded once, when the
    configuration is first loaded, and stored whole; an open panel never asks
    Drive for a listing, so the list appears instantly.
  * Write when the site is left. An edit made on an allowed site is applied to
    the cached list at once and kept in a durable queue; the Drive write waits
    until the tab is closed or hidden, then one full read brings the cache back
    in step. No timer writes anything earlier. A queue left by a browser that
    was quit is sent on the next start, unless an allowed site is still open;
    a write Drive refuses permanently is dropped from the queue.
  * Never sync while a site is open. The background check and the queue both
    stand down while any allowed site has a visible tab.
  * Make the toolbar icon a toggle. It now opens the side panel and closes it
    again (Chrome 141+), through sidePanel.setPanelBehavior, the same approach
    as the user's Yousub extension.
  * Remove the panel's own Close button: the toolbar icon is the switch.

