pastex (1.10.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Decide the paste from the input focus instead of the window state.
    Muffin on a Cinnamon X11 session (wm=Mutter (Muffin)) reported
    state=normal for the whole 900 ms budget even though the window had been
    iconified, and the client window stays IsViewable while a reparenting WM
    unmaps the frame around it, so xwininfo could not answer either. Both
    checks therefore refused to send Ctrl+V on a machine where the minimize
    worked. What the paste actually needs is the focus back on the target
    application, so the active window is now read with xdotool every 120 ms
    (a frame that still belongs to Pastex is recognised through its WM_CLASS)
    and that verdict decides the paste. WM_STATE and xwininfo remain the
    fallback when xdotool cannot answer.
  * Treat a viewable client window as "cannot tell" rather than "still on
    screen", and log the focus verdict, the mechanism that decided the paste
    and the observed focus in the give-up line.
  * Do not report an empty clipboard read-back as a mismatch: xclip forks the
    owner that takes the selection over, so pastex --check now re-reads once
    before judging and explains an empty clipboard instead.

