pastex (1.10.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the paste work on a machine whose window manager ignores the
    minimize request. 1.10.2 restored the window but never sent Ctrl+V,
    because iconify() did nothing at all: the state stayed "normal" for the
    whole 600 ms budget. The hide step now unmaximizes first (Tk/X11 drops
    iconify() for a zoomed window and puts the zoom back on restore), then, if
    the state still says normal, asks the window manager to minimize through
    xdotool's EWMH request, and finally asks the X server itself (xwininfo)
    whether the window is really unmapped -- a window manager that lags or
    skips WM_STATE then no longer costs the paste. The budget is 900 ms and
    the give-up line logs the Tk state, the X verdict, whether the WM was
    asked and whether the window was zoomed.
  * Name the window manager. The ready: line logs the window manager (or
    "none"), XDG_SESSION_TYPE and XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP, and pastex --check
    prints the same, because without a window manager nothing can minimize
    the window and automatic paste is not available at all.
  * Stop a picker paste from waiting for the main window. A popup paste
    destroys the popup and leaves the main window visible on purpose, but the
    hide check read the main window's state and gave up after 900 ms without
    sending Ctrl+V. The check skips the state for a popup paste.
  * Refresh the tree without inotify. When inotify cannot be opened the
    watcher falls back to polling the folders every 2 s instead of switching
    to manual refresh only, and the log names the errno.

