pastex (1.8.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Never leave the window minimized when Ctrl+V cannot be delivered. A click
    now arms a 9 s watchdog: if the send stage overruns it, the window comes
    back, the remaining tools are abandoned (so no key press can land in
    Pastex afterwards) and the failure dialog says why. Every tool call in the
    send stage now has its own timeout (2 s per keystroke, 6 s for the portal
    consent dialog), and an exception in either worker thread is reported
    instead of leaving the window hidden.
  * Start a private ydotoold when the user unit is missing. Ubuntu ships
    ydotoold.service as a system unit, so "systemctl --user start
    ydotoold.service" fails on a stock install and automatic paste never
    worked; Pastex now starts ydotoold itself with a socket it owns in
    XDG_RUNTIME_DIR and points ydotool at it through YDOTOOL_SOCKET. Only
    /dev/uinput access is still required, which --enable-permissions sets up.
  * Stop hiding the window once a paste has failed: the next click copies the
    text, keeps the window visible and shows the manual Ctrl+V hint, instead
    of minimizing and immediately bouncing back.
  * verify-regressions runs pytest with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE so a cached
    .pyc can no longer make a restored bug look like a passing test.

